{:event/id "dd9922c9-b08b-41a4-b817-b8507145e990" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:261aa432-7eb8-47d8-b3da-e098eac4509e" :event/seq 1 :event/causes ["261aa432-7eb8-47d8-b3da-e098eac4509e"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:261aa432-7eb8-47d8-b3da-e098eac4509e" :event/at "2026-09-17T13:36:13Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/resource-writes-form-keyed-serial-promise-lanes :finding/shapes #{:queue :cell :reconciler} :finding/current-name "resource-write-tails* + enqueue-resource-write! + run-after-resource-write!/retire-resource-write-tail!" :finding/candidate-name "KeyedSerialLane<Key,Effect>" :finding/claim "Knoxx serializes the complete resource-write transaction by exact file path using one process-local promise tail per key. A new task waits for the previous tail, but the stored recovery tail consumes predecessor rejection so one failed write does not poison later work. Tail retirement is compare-by-identity: an older completion removes the map entry only when it is still the current tail. Focused concurrency tests prove that a later write to the same path cannot snapshot or mutate until the earlier admission settles, then observes the exact bytes left by that predecessor. This is keyed in-process effect ordering, not a durable queue or history."}}
{:event/id "c3f92ee8-bc3b-414a-94b0-66b46e2e5488" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:261aa432-7eb8-47d8-b3da-e098eac4509e" :event/seq 2 :event/causes ["dd9922c9-b08b-41a4-b817-b8507145e990"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:261aa432-7eb8-47d8-b3da-e098eac4509e" :event/at "2026-09-17T13:36:13Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/resource-write-index-sync-is-compensation-bounded :finding/shapes #{:store :projection :reconciler} :finding/current-name "write-resource-and-admit-once! + rollback-resource-write! + require-index-sync!" :finding/candidate-name "CompensatedProjectionWrite<Source,Projection>" :finding/claim "Before admission, a resource mutation snapshots the prior file state, writes the requested bytes, and requires a successful resource-index synchronization. A write or forward-index failure compensates by restoring the prior bytes, or deleting a newly created file, and then synchronizing the index again before the original failure escapes; rollback failure is surfaced separately. This independently pressure-tests the earlier ReviewCommitBoundary law outside translation: compensation is justified only across the reversible source-plus-projection phase, not across every downstream effect."}}
{:event/id "8364982e-e4ed-4ec6-adf1-30a5c5f16469" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:261aa432-7eb8-47d8-b3da-e098eac4509e" :event/seq 3 :event/causes ["c3f92ee8-bc3b-414a-94b0-66b46e2e5488"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:261aa432-7eb8-47d8-b3da-e098eac4509e" :event/at "2026-09-17T13:36:13Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/admission-crosses-source-retaining-irreversible-cut :finding/shapes #{:reconciler :projection :ledger} :finding/current-name "write-resource-and-admit-once! admission boundary" :finding/candidate-name "SourceRetainingEffectCut<Source,Effect>" :finding/claim "Admission begins only after source bytes and their resource index projection are synchronized. Because admission may append durable events or enqueue agents before reporting failure, Knoxx deliberately does not roll the file back once admission has begun. Tests require both replacement and newly created source bytes to remain after admission rejection, so retry or reconciliation retains the exact source that may already have caused irreversible effects. The law is a source-retaining cut between compensatable mutation and potentially escaped effects, not generic transaction rollback."}}
